{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr49Zr3WbA2TrpVLbx8r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't open the source, so this diagnosis is inferred from the symptom and the symbol names. I haven't confirmed the line ranges.\n\nThe symptom points to an off-by-one-page offset. Page 1 skips 10 users, and page 2 starts at the 21st. That matches an offset of `page * limit` where it should be `(page - 1) * limit`. With only two seeded users, skipping 10 rows returns nothing.\n\nThe offset is most likely computed in the repository's `findManyWithPagination`. The relational (TypeORM) repository is the likelier candidate. The document (Mongoose) repository has the same method and could carry the same flaw."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4748,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"870e4836-fb89-4743-93b4-e1d247690230","uuid":"e96f3e16-3ee7-46d5-968e-02334f5ab052","timestamp":"2026-11-08T20:00:21.846Z","request_id":"req_011Cgr49ZaffF8Pvn658Jc7d"}
